s, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186314809 :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=t \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)-{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+t \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t